 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "The big fppf site",
 "statement": "Let $S$ be a scheme and $\\mathit{Sch}_{fppf}$ a big fppf site containing\n$S$ (Topologies, Definition 34.7.8, Tag\n[021S](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/021S)). The\n*big fppf site of $S$* is $(\\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$, whose coverings\nare the families $\\{T_i\\to T\\}_{i\\in I}$ of\nflat morphisms locally of finite\npresentation; an *fppf covering* is such a family.",
